  "generated_text": "To find \\(\\det (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B})\\), we will use the property of determinants that states the determinant of the product of two matrices is the product of their determinants. Mathematically, this is expressed as:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B}) = \\det \\mathbf{A} \\cdot \\det \\mathbf{B}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\det \\mathbf{A} = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\det \\mathbf{B} = 12\n\\]\n\nWe substitute the given values into the property:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B}) = 2 \\cdot 12\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n2 \\cdot 12 = 24\n\\]\n\nThus, the determinant of the product \\(\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\det (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B}) = 24\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[24, '24']",
    "gold_answer": "We have that $\\det (\\mathbf{A} \\mathbf{B}) = (\\det \\mathbf{A})(\\det \\mathbf{B}) = (2)(12) = \\boxed{24}.$",
    "is_correct": true
  },
